      "side": 1,
      "message": "Pre-commit hook can silently block commits when token is missing\n\nIn the pre-commit hook if SOCKET_CLI_API_TOKEN is not set, the script only prints a warning but still runs socket ci — which will fail with an auth error and block the commit with a confusing error. The hook should exit 0 (skip the scan) when no token is available:\n\n```\nif [ -z \"$SOCKET_CLI_API_TOKEN\" ]; then\n  echo \"Warning: SOCKET_CLI_API_TOKEN not set — skipping Socket scan.\"\n  exit 0\nfi\n```",
